# Second git dir. This working tree is covered by two repos: this one (publish-safe,
# see the privacy boundary below) and a full-tree private backup that deliberately
# DOES include the paths that boundary excludes. See scripts/backup-private.sh.
.git-private/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Privacy boundary — this repo is the public extraction of a private vault app.
#
# The paths below exist in the private source repo and MUST NOT be published.
# They are listed here rather than merely left unstaged so that a careless
# `git add -A` cannot publish them: the ignore rule is the guard, not discipline.
#
# `src/data/generated/` is the one deliberate exception to that pattern. It IS
# tracked here, but every file in it is a synthetic demo fixture — invented
# content in the real schema — because `src/data/vaultApi.js` imports them
# statically, so a clone with no fixtures cannot build. This is safe precisely
# because the sync script that would regenerate them from a real vault is not
# shipped (see ARCHITECTURE.md). Never overwrite them with synced output.
#
# `os/hooks/` is the SECOND deliberate exception, added 2026-08-17. It holds code
# copied out of the private vault's `.claude/scripts/` — i.e. material this
# boundary would otherwise cover — and it IS tracked. Stated plainly here so the
# exception is visible at the boundary rather than discovered later:
#
#   - Scope is a fixed, reviewed list: 5 hook scripts + their 14-module import
#     closure. It is not "the scripts directory"; do not widen it by copying more
#     in without re-running the review.
#   - Every file was scanned for career, compensation, client, credential and
#     personal content before landing. The only hits were two *filenames* inside
#     hint strings. Re-run that scan before adding anything.
#   - `settings.json` is deliberately NOT shipped, so nothing under `os/` is wired
#     or runnable from a clone. It is readable evidence, not an install.
#   - Excluded on purpose: session-start.ts and stop-checklist.ts (vault-specific),
#     check-broad-git-staging.ts (wired to no hook — shipping it would imply
#     autonomy that isn't running).
#
# The ignore rule cannot be the guard for this one, so the review is. If that
# tradeoff ever stops being worth it, ignore `os/` here and delete the directory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
branding/
memory-bank/
scripts/
skills/
CLAUDE.md
USER.md
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real vault data — the ONLY place it may live in this repo, and it never
# enters git. src/data/vaultApi.js prefers these files at runtime and falls
# back to the tracked synthetic fixtures in src/data/generated/ when absent,
# so a fresh clone still builds and runs. Written by scripts/sync-vault-data.mjs.
#
# Do not "fix" a missing dashboard by copying real data into src/data/generated/
# — that path is tracked, and that is exactly how real tasks got published once.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/data/local/
